### GM-16 local GoTrue; never paste credentials into this tracked file.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:54321
@publicKey = {{$processEnv SUPABASE_ANON_KEY}}
@accessToken = {{$processEnv GM16_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
@refreshToken = {{$processEnv GM16_REFRESH_TOKEN}}

### Create synthetic guest: expect 200, real user.id, is_anonymous=true,
### access_token/refresh_token nonempty, expires_in>0; metadata.userId is NOT caller.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"data":{"display_name":"GM16 test","userId":"16000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"}}

### Restore identity: expect 200; id equals guest.id, not spoofed metadata.userId.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### No session: expect 401/403, no private user response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
apikey: {{publicKey}}

### Forged token: expect 401/403, never caller success.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Authorization: Bearer deliberately.invalid.token

### Refresh: expect 200, same user.id, new usable tokens; never log response secrets.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=refresh_token
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"refresh_token":"{{refreshToken}}"}

### Invalid refresh: expect 400/401, auth error normalized to AUTH_REQUIRED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=refresh_token
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"refresh_token":"not-a-refresh-token"}

### Logout current session: expect 204 (or 200 body supported by server version).
### Subsequent refresh must fail. Already-issued access JWT can live until expiry.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/logout?scope=local
apikey: {{publicKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Automated assertions: node scripts/gm16_auth_check.mjs
### --rate-limit adds a bounded real HTTP429 probe; use isolated local demo only.
### --sql runs auth.sql via this project's DB container; transaction rolls back.
### Do not infer secure storage/native restart from this HTTP collection.
